A||||25||FieroLisa||Wisconsin Dells Show! :)||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||06-03-2001||08:42 PM||||Just got in from the Dells Show this weekend, tons of fun. 126 fieros were shown, and there were 12 or 14 outside of the show. Half the participants got trophies (including me, yay!!!) and all around was a great weekend. One other trophy that was passed out was the hard luck...Archie got it no contest for not having the pins in his rear glass in the Fino secured...basically destroying his Fino and Finale, which was driving behind. But he did have a lot of his LT1s there that did well. <BR>Chula Vista was excellent!!!! I wish the weather cooperated more,it was about 50 degrees or less with drizzle all day.  But when the rain cleared a bunch of us went go karting and pretty much destroyed the tracks!! (and I kicked som @ss, right Fierohoho  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) <BR>So I can't wait to go again next year, and will have lots of pics up on the website tonight or tomorrow!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR> <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jaei Sun||06-03-2001||09:53 PM||||The Dells show was pretty good.  I was one of the 12-14 cars outside the show (next year I'll show with my new paint).  My favorite was the Audi Cream White GT.  That car looked so nice and the interior was hands down awesome!  I’ll post the URL to the pix I took in the future… I ended up taking 17 MB worth of pictures… beautiful cars everywhere!<P>Anyone here hear about Jimmy's bad luck with his black GT?  Well for those who didn't hear his GT's Clutch Hydraulic line at the slave leaked out after he got to the show.  Thanks to those who contributed help/tools to try to fix it.  And a big no-thanks to Wisconsin Dell’s, for not having ANY hardware or automotive stores open on Sundays (how lame is that??!?!?). So we were limited to jerry-riggin &lt;sp?&gt;.  So on Sunday Morning we attempted to fix the line using parts elsewhere from the car.  We tried using the small diameter coolant hoses that are attached to the throttle body lines.  BUT that didn’t work too well so Jim wanted to try driving the car without a clutch.  Running start launches, matching rpms required…:P.  So for the most part it he got it running and was on his way back home.<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jaei Sun (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000002||Archie||06-03-2001||10:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>The Dells show was pretty good.  My favorite was the Audi Cream White GT.  That car looked so nice and the interior was hands down awesome!  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here it is <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-333s.jpg"> <P>Powered by ZZ-4 Chevy Crate engine with TPI. We just finished the engine installation Thursday and he drove it to the Dells on Friday.<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bluebottlejunky||06-03-2001||10:31 PM||||Yup it was a pretty sweet show Lisa, nice meeting you too...didn't talk much lol 1st im shy 2nd you were busy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||6
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||06-03-2001||10:35 PM||||What about the Ferrari Rebody??  I thought that was pretty awesome.  I have a few pics that I can put on a page or send to some one if they want to see them.  Also have pics of the 'Dark Knight' hood, and of the Convertible that was there.  Was hoping to find more parts venders there than there was.<BR>Oh, I had fun.||||reg||1
